<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 58,177 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 58,177 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 58,177 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 48,558 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			20,729	   19,565</p>
<p>    Import cargo			37,448	   28,993</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Mogas		    25,000	 Athenian Success    due</p>
<p>Chemicals		 3,000	 Owl Trader	   27/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 50,000	 Al-Marwah	    26/5</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		 20/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Ying Song Hu	 30/5</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    7,000	 Patty Anne	    due</p>
<p>Vegoil		    8,000	 Ariston		23/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
